# Secrets
.env
.amap_key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw Overpass responses, ~24MB and entirely rebuildable: delete the folder and
# `python basemap/build_basemap.py` fetches them again. The basemap built from
# them is OpenStreetMap's (ODbL), not the guide's, so this is bulk rather than
# a rights question.
basemap/cache/

# --- The guide, and everything derived from it -------------------------------
# This repo publishes the code only. The guide is Christopher St. Cavish's paid
# work: neither the PDF nor anything extracted from it belongs in a public repo.
# Run the pipeline against your own copy to produce these locally.
#
# NOTE: git history is forever. If any of these are ever committed by accident,
# deleting them in a later commit is not enough — the blob stays in history and
# the branch has to be rewritten.
*.pdf
data/*
!data/README.md

# The builds. dist/Eating-in-Shanghai.html inlines every restaurant record and,
# in the buyer edition, the guide's prose in full -- it is the most concentrated
# copy of his writing this repo can produce. dist/site/ carries the same data as
# separate files. Both are rebuildable in seconds from `python build/build_dist.py`,
# so there is no reason to track either.
dist/

# Working notes: candid, and they quote the guide directly. PLAN.md is the same
# deal — it names the author and discusses an arrangement that is not agreed.
NOTES.md
PLAN.md

# Share assets: screenshots contain extracts of the guide's text. Un-ignore
# these only once the author has agreed to them appearing in the README.
share/
